Subject: [PATCH] R80b, part 6, patch 15 (cld-advisor, at main's word in M16;
 main's third folder, section 2, row A13): B1880'S LOCK HOLDS WHAT ITS TWO
 SCRIPTS SAY AND WRITE, AND THE KEPT RUN SAYS WHICH RUN IT IS

A reader's check of main's answers at Review 80 (agy-002's; row A13; main held the kept run's last line and
did not check the lock). The docstrings of B1880's two scripts were corrected, and the lock reads neither,
so either mend put back passes. And the kept run of the measuring script ends with the line of a run made
with --write.

Made again here: the lock passes with the corrected bracket taken out of either docstring.

The lock now holds:
  - the sentences of the two docstrings that the corrections wrote, and the old words each keeps;
  - that each script does what its docstring says. The measuring script writes three files: the frozen list
    under --write, and the folder's two outputs under --keep-outputs. The reading script writes its run
    under --write. Each write is found in the script's own tree, with the conditions it stands under.
Five planted changes are reported: the bracket taken out of each docstring; the measuring script said again
to write at every run; the folder's outputs written at every run again; the reading script made to write
at every call.

THE KEPT RUN has one dated line added at its end. It says that the line above it is the line of a run made
with --write; that the run kept was made so on the day the arc landed, when the script still wrote this
file at every run; and that a run without --write ends before that line and writes nothing. That is the
builder's reading of the script's own history, and is main's to correct. Nothing else of the file is changed.

The lock passes: 10 tests. Every gate passes but the count of landings.
Not checked by main as to the lock. Tested against planted errors by the session that wrote it.
